notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T13:32:23.768Z",pi-agent,"Resolved 18 CodeRabbit findings on PR 7. Applied 13, declined 5 with recorded reasons. Substantive fixes: shared GateResult + runIfMain in script-launcher.ts (removed the 3-way duplicated array-index dispatch and its dead arrows); realpath-based isMainInvocation comparison (Windows drive-letter casing); SIGKILL escalation with injectable escalationMs in streamProcess; case-insensitive allowlist matching + masked rejection reporting in auditGitIdentities; bounded npx tsc --showConfig (--no-install + 60s timeout); JSON.parse guard restating the refusing-to-guess diagnostic; parseLcov narrowed to an existsSync guard so read errors stay honest; showConfig threaded through runGate and main; Windows shell executable path quoting in prepare-merge-driver; trailing-newline on docstring-gate main output; npm tarball narrowed (files: dist/index.*, dist/series.*) so release scripts no longer publish. Test fixes: imported DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS (single source of truth), added JSON-guard/showConfig-threading/SIGKILL/maskAddress/runIfMain/docstring-success tests. Coverage 100/100/100 across 8 source files (92 tests pass). Declined 5 trivial test-stub extractions (jscpd ignores test/, inline stubs are locally explicit) and the POSIX-only prepare test (ubuntu-only CI; unique end-to-end coverage of the default installer). Redacted the restated authoring address from pm-rl-zcqf narrative records via pm history-redact (allowlist untouched by design). Mutation-verified each touched gate still fails on a real violation: audit (drop stefan@preu.at -> rejects s***@preu.at exit 1), coverage (uncovered branch -> 99.85/99.12 exit 1), docstring (undocumented export -> exit 1)."
